# Cloudflare Access identity (see docs/authentication.md). CF_ACCESS_TEAM_DOMAIN is the
# Zero Trust team name (the <team> in <team>.cloudflareaccess.com); CF_ACCESS_AUD is the
# Access application's AUD tag. Both are non-secret configuration.
# CF_ACCESS_TEAM_DOMAIN=
# CF_ACCESS_AUD=
# Dropbox OAuth — sign-in identity for gallery editors. Create an app at
# https://www.dropbox.com/developers/apps and set these in .env.local for dev
# (or as Worker secrets for production). Register the callback URL
# http://localhost:5173/auth/dropbox/callback (dev) and
# https://manorama.xyz/auth/dropbox/callback (prod) in the Dropbox app console.
# DROPBOX_APP_KEY=
# DROPBOX_APP_SECRET=
# Google sign-in (optional until the owner configures it) — a Google Cloud
# Web OAuth client; register https://manorama.xyz/auth/google/callback as an
# authorized redirect URI. /auth/google answers /?error=1 while unset.
# GOOGLE_AUTH_CLIENT_ID=
# GOOGLE_AUTH_CLIENT_SECRET=
# Apple sign-in (optional until the owner configures it) — a Sign in with
# Apple Services ID plus the ES256 key from a private key download.
# Register https://manorama.xyz/auth/apple/callback as a return URL.
# APPLE_CLIENT_ID=
# APPLE_TEAM_ID=
# APPLE_KEY_ID=
# APPLE_PRIVATE_KEY=
# Signs the manorama_session cookie (HS256 JWT). Set in .env.local for dev
# and as a Worker secret for production.
# HOST_API_JWT_SECRET=
# Billing webhooks — all three are Worker secrets. REVENUECAT_WEBHOOK_AUTH is
# the Authorization header value configured in the RevenueCat dashboard; the
# signing secrets verify each provider's HMAC. RevenueCat HMAC signing must be
# enabled in the dashboard and the matching REVENUECAT_WEBHOOK_SIGNING_SECRET
# deployed before release — without it every delivery receives 401. Both
# webhook endpoints fail closed until theirs are set, never open.
# REVENUECAT_WEBHOOK_AUTH=
# REVENUECAT_WEBHOOK_SIGNING_SECRET=
# STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SIGNING_SECRET=
# Dev-seed sample sources (vite.config.ts manoramaDevSeed): each var set in
# .env.local is live-scanned at dev boot into a seeded gallery —
# ICLOUD → /thecontrarian/mixed-album, MEGA → dev-mega, DROPBOX → dev-dropbox,
# GDRIVE → dev-gdrive. Public share links, not secrets — but keep them in
# .env.local (gitignored) since they're personal albums, and quote any value
# containing a # fragment. MANORAMA_DEV_VIDEO_URL is the older name for the
# iCloud slot and still works.
# MANORAMA_DEV_SOURCE_ICLOUD=
# MANORAMA_DEV_SOURCE_MEGA=
# MANORAMA_DEV_SOURCE_DROPBOX=
# MANORAMA_DEV_SOURCE_GDRIVE=
# Native RevenueCat public SDK key (safe to ship in the client; use the test key
# for local sandbox builds and a platform-specific public key for production).
# VITE_REVENUECAT_API_KEY=
# Desktop share/upload provider OAuth — PUBLIC app identifiers (not secrets)
# for the desktop client's own Dropbox/Google grants, distinct from the
# sign-in apps above. Setup steps are in docs/desktop-uploads.md. Unset =
# that provider shows "not configured in this build" in the share sheet.
# MANORAMA_DESKTOP_DROPBOX_CLIENT_ID=
# MANORAMA_DESKTOP_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
# Optional: the Google desktop client's public-by-design secret, if your
# client type requires it at exchange time (most desktop clients do not).
# MANORAMA_DESKTOP_GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
# Opt-in local D1 for `bun run dev` — boots a persisted wrangler platform
# proxy (.wrangler/state/v3) with every migration applied and serves it as
# the request path's DB binding via injectDevD1. Without it, repositories
# use in-memory Maps and real provider OAuth cannot finish: auth_identities
# deliberately has no memory fallback, so sign-in needs this flag. The dev
# seed writes through the same binding, and /.dev-seed/reset wipes the
# local tables.
# MANORAMA_DEV_D1=
# Master resolution in dev — identical to production: MASTER_ACCOUNT_ID is
# the bootstrap account outright; MASTER_DROPBOX_SUBJECT resolves through
# auth_identities, so a real Dropbox sign-in carrying that subject lands
# with operations access (e.g. /opman). Neither is set by default.
# MASTER_ACCOUNT_ID=
# MASTER_DROPBOX_SUBJECT=
# Temporary migration-only capability for the legacy encrypted cohort.
# "enabled" lets the retired /api/mega/file and /api/mega/preview endpoints
# serve keyed manifests again; any other value (or unset) returns
# SERVER_DECRYPT_RETIRED. Enable only for the cohort-migration window in the
# environment doing the migration, then remove — the default must stay retired.
# LEGACY_ENCRYPTED_DECRYPT=
